  "verbalization": "Fosaprepitant, a neurokinin 1 antagonist, is linked to Tacr1 through a shared binding interaction with Aprepitant, which is included in the class of neurokinin 1 antagonists. This suggests a potential mechanism by which Fosaprepitant may influence Tacr1, possibly through a common pathway involving Aprepitant. The evidence from multiple paths indicates that Fosaprepitant may act via Aprepitant to modulate Tacr1, with Aprepitant serving as a bridge between the drug and the receptor. The lowest common ancestor of Fosaprepitant and Aprepitant points to the antiemetic agent class, highlighting a shared functional role in treating nausea and vomiting. The integration of these paths supports the notion that Fosaprepitant and Tacr1 are connected through a mechanism involving Aprepitant, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
